rota lap 4474, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; advanced by hand past Earth, which this seat read last lap. Its dual seat, the grain and the crossing, carries the ear rule the fusion seated -- a guard that cannot red guards nothing, and a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything. That sentence chose the lap.
think Five of the fifty-three guards standing_equipment_redleg names sit in my lane. I took glow_shop_core, which watches looks_like_shop_core -- the predicate deciding whether a `|%` source lowers down the welcome road or the shop's -- because it is the most Lindy of the five: a language's own road-picking rule outlives every desk that travels it.
think The subject needs a compiler, so the pen is a checkout plus three links. A git worktree carries every tracked file; rye/bin, rishi/bin and vendor/zig-toolchain are ignored build outputs, and the zig alone is 165 MB, so the pen links them back rather than paying that per plant. Runner, module and selftest are copied in from disk, so a repair is proven in its new form.
think One shape the peer's control did not have to solve: my control runs the WITNESS, and the witness now runs the control. The pen's runner is cut at a `# CONTROL LEG` marker, and the cut refuses out loud if the marker is absent -- the one place the pen copy departs from disk, named where a reader meets it.
think Three plants in the module and the selftest exits non-zero, which proves the DELEGATE can sound. That is the whole of what a delegating guard's own file was ever asked for, and it says nothing about the runner's seventeen legs. So the fourth plant left a selftest exiting 0 with one claim line reworded, and only the runner's own text legs could catch it. That one bit, at line 37.
think The fifth plant refused nothing, and that is the lap's finding. `assert selftest.out contains "GREEN"` reads a delegate whose every leg line ends `-- GREEN`, so it matched the first leg; the closing summary could be renamed or deleted whole and the guard still read green. A leg that cannot fail is a leg that was never there.
obs The same shape stands one file over, written down and left as prose. glow_vane_pair_mirrors_witness.rish records in its own `20260828` header that `contains` is a substring test and the worker's own EXIT:0 tail contains a 0, which is how an elder blindness survived. Two firings in one family, and no reading was ever made of it -- a lantern that fires twice.
obs The class is named rather than claimed: 1,375 `contains "GREEN"` sites across 819 tracked .rish files, 35 in rostered guards. A site is vacuous only where the delegate prints GREEN beside its summary, and that discriminator wants each delegate RUN rather than grepped, so the count is a population and not a defect count. A meter, if Keaton wants one.
obs I left the redleg ceiling at 53 with the reading at 52. Lowering with no slack is the ratchet's own habit and it re-arms exactly the fleet-wide refusal `%670` measured yesterday, on a question Keaton has open. Named on the card rather than taken.
obs The control is proven able to fail three ways rather than one: 18 checks against the repaired runner, 16 with two failures against the elder summary leg, and pass=17 fail=1 under a mutated expectation. A refusal shown only in the failing direction cannot be told from a tool that refuses everything, so every plant is lifted and read back.
obs Against myself: the first draft's baseline leg asserted on a decline line the runner never prints, because the runner CAPTURES the selftest's output rather than echoing it -- the same reading limit the two text plants exploit, met from the wrong side. Caught by running the draft, at 15 of 18.
